  "notes": [
    "fixture 7 in docs/EVALUATION.md \u00a72",
    "after_mutation=unknown models the TTL-expiry case; no world mutation required",
    "There is deliberately no input_probes block: no probe ships for web.search and none can, so this scenario also pins the engine's volatile rule from ARCHITECTURE.md \u00a77 \u2014 inside TTL is likely-valid, outside is unknown. The harness advances its injected clock past ttl_seconds to reach after_mutation.",
    "This scenario registers no probe, so it IS ADR 0009's no-probe-registered arm: the edge is inside a validated TTL and nothing checked it. Post-W9.1 that carries `volatile-within-ttl-unprobed`, not `trust-class-volatile-caps-at-likely-valid` \u2014 the latter asserts a probe ran and agreed. Same verdict, different evidence, and the certificate has to say which.",
    "This is the UNPROBED arm; volatile-external-dep-probed is the probed arm. Their `value` fields are deliberately identical and their `reason_codes` deliberately are NOT. The identical VALUE is the assertion \u2014 ADR 0009 Amendment 2's guarantee that registering a probe cannot by itself move a volatile edge's verdict, only positive drift evidence can. The differing REASON is W9.1's: same verdict, different evidence, and the certificate must say which. Before W9.1 both blocks were identical and the notes said that identity was the assertion; when the reason codes split, the pair silently stopped pinning the verdict guarantee it existed for. `the_probed_and_unprobed_volatile_arms_agree_on_the_verdict` in crates/freshdag-engine/src/tests.rs now pins it directly, because a note is not a test."
  ]
